      "title": "Kirloskar Industries Q2 profit rises 5% to ₹105 crore, income up 17%",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/kirloskar-industries-q2-profit-rises-5-to-105-crore-income-up-17-126110701228_1.html",
      "description": "Kirloskar Industries Ltd (KIL) has reported a 5 per cent rise in consolidated profit after tax to Rs 105 crore in the quarter ended September 2026.\nThe company had posted a consolidated PAT (profit after tax) of Rs 100.1 crore in the year-ago period.\nConsolidated income of the company during the second quarter rose to Rs 2,097.7 crore from Rs 1,790.1 crore in the year-ago period, KIL said in a statement.\n\"Our material subsidiary, Kirloskar Ferrous Industries Limited, continued to deliver a resilient performance during the year, supported by operational stability, capacity optimisation and strong demand for its products across the sectors. On the real estate front, our wholly-owned subsidiary, Avante Spaces Limited (ASL), is progressing well.\nOur landmark Kothrud project is going well and moving forward on track, reinforcing our vision of creating premium, future-ready spaces that maximise value for our stakeholders,\" George Verghese, Managing Director, KIL, said.\nKirloskar Industr",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-07T16:37:31"
    },
    {
      "title": "Tata Steel Q2 net profit up 18.2 per cent Y-o-Y, led by India operations",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/tata-steel-q2-fy27-results-net-profit-india-operations-uk-netherlands-126110700767_1.html",
